Vraw_src raw_in N001 24
Dpol raw_in vraw_pol D_generic
Rfuse VRAW vraw_pol 0.05
Cbulk VRAW 0 470µ
Rvg1 VRAW vg_sense 10k
Rvg2 vg_sense 0 10k
Cvg vg_sense 0 200µ
X§Xvg vg_sense VGND VRAW 0 VGND IDEAL_OPAMP ;§pnba In+)In-)V+)V-)OUT
Imotor_load 0 0 PULSE(0 200m 2m 10u 10u 50m 100m)
V_ripple N001 0 SINE(0 0.1 60) AC 1
.model D D
.lib C:\Users\Umart\AppData\Local\LTspice\lib\cmp\standard.dio
.model D_generic D(IS=1e-9 RS=0.05 N=1.05 BV=100)
* .op
* .tran 0 1000m 0 10u
.subckt IDEAL_OPAMP inP inN vp vn out
Ein out 0 inP inN 1MEG
Rin_ideal inP inN 1G
.ends IDEAL_OPAMP
* Power Supply - single 24V input, virtual-ground split for the audio (preamp) branch,\nisolated black-box load for the motor branch (schematic version of power_supply.cir).\nVraw_src = ideal stand-in for the COTS 24V DC brick.\nSAFETY-SENSITIVE: Dpol part/rating and fuse rating are PLACEHOLDERS - confirm with user.\nRfuse models normal-operation resistance only (no blow model).
* Virtual ground: divider + unity-gain buffer -> VGND.\nXvg uses IDEAL_OPAMP (supply pins drawn for the symbol, unused by the model);\nreplace with a real general-purpose op-amp or rail-splitter (e.g. TLE2426) when finalizing.
* Motor branch: BLACK BOX per motor-branch-interface-spec.md.\n0 -> 200mA step at t=2ms; watch V(VRAW), V(VGND) for sag.
* Integration: tie riaa_preamp "0" to VGND, VCC to VRAW, VEE to this sheet's 0 (PGND).
.ac dec 20 0.001 30000
.backanno
.end
